## Nyxuri SwayFX monitors configuration

# This file stores configurations (resolution, refresh rate, scale,position, etc) for all your display outputs.
# SwayFX will automatically set all detected monitors to proper modes, so there's no need to write anything here by default.
# To make custom modifications to specific monitors, see sway-output(5) and following examples


# Laptop internal display (1080p 144Hz)

# output eDP-1 {
# 	mode 1920x1080@144Hz
# 	scale 1
# 	position 0 0
# }


# External high refresh rate display (2k 165Hz, Variable Refresh Rate on, flipped landscape)

# output DP-1 {
# 	mode 2560x1440@165Hz
# 	scale 1
# 	adaptive_sync on
# 	position 1920 0
# 	transform 180
# }


# Virtual display (vkms, 720p 60Hz, 1.25x)

# output Virtual-1 {
# 	mode 1280x720@60Hz
# 	position 4480 0
# 	scale 1.25
# }
